vLLM 0.27.1: stop xgrammar token batches at grammar termination.

MTP speculative decoding can return a token batch whose grammar stop token is
followed by unused draft tokens. The matcher terminates on the stop token. The
old accept_tokens loop then feeds the following token to the terminated matcher,
which logs "Failed to advance FSM". validate_tokens has the same problem while
simulating draft tokens. Refresh the wrapper state immediately, treat calls on
an already-satisfied grammar as successful, and stop both loops at termination.
At a mid-window reasoning boundary, prevalidate old draft tokens quietly before
advancing the grammar because rejection is explicitly expected in that branch.

This is the v0.27.1 form of the defect tracked in:
  https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/42619
  https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/49210

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < xgrammar-terminated-batch.patch

--- a/v1/structured_output/backend_xgrammar.py
+++ b/v1/structured_output/backend_xgrammar.py
@@ -158,14 +158,23 @@ class XgrammarGrammar(StructuredOutputGrammar):
         if self._is_terminated:
-            return False
+            return True
         for token in tokens:
+            # An accepted stop token ends this speculative token batch.
             if not self.matcher.accept_token(token):
+                self._is_terminated = self.matcher.is_terminated()
+                if self._is_terminated:
+                    # validate_tokens may have reached the stop token while
+                    # simulating a draft window. xgrammar can retain that
+                    # terminal state after rollback; the grammar is satisfied.
+                    return True
                 logger.error(
                     "Failed to advance FSM for request %s "
                     "for tokens %s. Please file an issue.",
                     request_id,
                     token,
                 )
                 return False
             self.num_processed_tokens += 1
-        self._is_terminated = self.matcher.is_terminated()
+            self._is_terminated = self.matcher.is_terminated()
+            if self._is_terminated:
+                break
         return True
@@ -180,6 +189,9 @@ class XgrammarGrammar(StructuredOutputGrammar):
         for token in tokens:
             if self.matcher.accept_token(token):
                 accepted_tokens.append(token)
+                # Do not offer unused draft tokens after the grammar stop.
+                if self.matcher.is_terminated():
+                    break
             else:
                 break
         if len(accepted_tokens) > 0:

